--
N5008 [temp.spec.partial.match]/2-3: P<int, char, char> matches the
constrained partial specialization `P<A, Args...>' with Args = {char, char}.
The front end selects the primary template (n == 0); with one element the
more specialized `P<A, Arg>' is chosen.  The same shape as libstdc++'s
views::__adaptor::_Partial.  Not yet diagnosed.  Pre-existing (bin53).  g++
13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
